    "result_text": "The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), returning `UNKNOWN` otherwise. Three small, focused touches:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setLocality`.\n2. **`Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny cohesive helper mirroring the existing `MembershipTier` pattern: a private-constructor final class with a single static `of(Owner)` backed by an immutable `Map`, defaulting to `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 one added line, `dto.setLocality(Locality.of(owner))`, in the GET responder.\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: the derivation lives in a brand-new class with zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), and the only edited method (`RespondWithOwner.service`) is a straight-line method with one changed line. `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass including the two new locality tests (`NSW` for Sydney, `UNKNOWN` for an unknown city).",
